{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - I am the **PLANNING agent (Phase 1 of 2)**. I must NOT write implementation code. A separate implementation agent runs in a fresh session and inherits ONLY `/workspace/PLAN.md` — so PLAN.md must be concrete and fully self-contained.\n   - **Deliverable**: Write `/workspace/PLAN.md` with three sections:\n     1. **Engine gaps table**: `| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |` — for each mechanic, decide if engine already supports it (name the seam + an FDN card using it) or needs a new/extended capability (smallest shared change, prefer ONE shared seam reused by several cards).\n     2. **Per-card plan**: For each card — oracle clauses; nearest FDN analogue (`cards/fdn/<id>`); exact engine seam(s) to reuse; any new engine change (reference gap table); key edge cases worth a test.\n     3. **Implementation order**: Ordered list of cards + shared engine changes to make first, grouped by shared seam, foundational engine work before dependent cards, simplest→hardest, one-line rationale per group.\n   - **Underlying task** (for the implementer): Implement 10 SOS cards in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257), using FDN cards as examples, making additive engine changes as needed.\n   - **Constraints (verbatim, must be preserved)**: \"Do NOT edit any `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py` or `engine/` file in this phase. Planning only.\" From AGENTS.md: (1) Card location invariant — keep each card's class in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. (2) Staged-test integrity — \"Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only\" and \"do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`\" (may read, never edit). (3) Additive-only engine modifications — \"You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\" Also from prompt: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/.\" Own SOS tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG rules engine (pure Python). Imported as bare `engine` / `cards.sos.sos_N`.\n   - CardImpl hook methods: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int`, `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`. Land adds `get_mana_abilities`. Planeswalker adds `get_loyalty_abilities`.\n   - Trigger system: `TriggerManager.fire_event`, `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`, APNAP ordering. Events in events.py.\n   - Replacement effects: `ReplacementManager.apply`, `ReplacementEffect(event_type, source, condition, replacement, controller)`, \"instead\" semantics, subtype matching.\n   - Casting: `cast_spell` (pays mana, stores `card.colors_spent`), `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` (no mana/timing), `get_cost_reduction`/`_apply_cost_reduction` (only generic reduction, only queries card's own hook).\n   - `copy_spell(game, original, controller, new_targets)` in stack.py (for Casualty/copies).\n   - Continuous effects / 7-layer system: `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, `EffectManager.add/apply_all/remove_expired`. DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0. `apply_all` resets battlefield objects then reapplies; only auto-called in cleanup.\n   - Combat: `declare_attackers_step` (does NOT fire attack triggers — gap).\n   - Turn loop: `run_turn`, only fires `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` (no player). No main-phase begin event.\n   - Mana: `ManaPool.add/pay/can_pay`, `last_payment_colors` (Converge). Mana types restriction not modeled.\n   - SBAs in state_based_actions.py: legend rule exists; NO planeswalker-0-loyalty SBA.\n   - `extra_turns: list[int]` FIFO queue (no skip mechanism). No coin-flip helper.\n   - Custom keywords needed: Converge, Prepared, Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity (for creatures).\n   - Test helpers: `create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game, player_index, battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana=)`, `cast_spell(game, idx, name, targets=)`, `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers`, `declare_blockers`, `DeterministicPlayer` (scripted choices). FDN cards with tests: fdn_13, fdn_142, fdn_205, fdn_215, fdn_244.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md` & `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`: Rules and layout. Constraints above.\n   - `/workspace/engine/card.py`: CardImpl + subclasses (Creature, Instant, Sorcery, Enchantment, Aura, Artifact, ArtifactCreature, Planeswalker w/ `starting_loyalty`/`loyalty`/`get_loyalty_abilities`, Land w/ `get_mana_abilities`). Hook `cost_reduction(game)->int` returns generic reduction (clamped ≥0, only generic). `register_triggers`/`register_replacement_effects` hooks. Creature has base/modified power/toughness, counters, `_reset_characteristics`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py`: Triggered events incl. `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` (UNFIRED), `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` (UNFIRED), `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired, no fields), `DrawsCardTriggeredEvent`. Replacement events: `MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent(destination, controller, owner, prevented)` + subclasses; `destination` redirect via strings \"graveyard\"/\"exile\"/\"hand\"/\"library\".\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py`: `cast_spell` pipeline (timing→can_cast→hand→stack→targets→protection→cost reduction→pay→colors_spent→on_cast→push). `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)`. `_resolve_spell` sets `card.chosen_targets`, moves permanents to battlefield / inst-sorc to graveyard via `move_to_zone`. `get_cost_reduction` only queries `card.cost_reduction(game)`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/zones.py`: `move_to_zone(game, card, from_zone, to_zone, replacement_event=None)` — replacement on battlefield-leave, fires LTB/CreatureDies, registers triggers/replacements on ETB AFTER firing ETB event.\n   - `/workspace/engine/mana.py`: `last_payment_colors` computed by old/new pool diff; auto-pay generic prefers colorless.\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py`: `advance_phase`, `extra_turns` FIFO, `_normal_next_index`, `_TURN_SEQUENCE` (main phases are `(PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None)`/`(POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None)`).\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py`: `run_turn` fires only upkeep event; `_do_cleanup_step` calls `effect_manager.remove_expired` + `apply_all`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py`: `declare_attackers_step` taps attackers (not vigilance), sets `is_attacking` — does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent.\n   - `/workspace/engine/abilities.py`: `activate_ability`, `LoyaltyAbilityInstance` (sorcery-speed, once/turn via `_loyalty_activated_this_turn`), `clear_loyalty_tracking`, `tap_cost`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py`: legend rule SBA; no PW-loyalty SBA.\n   - `/workspace/engine/continuous_effects.py`: Layer enum (COPY=1...POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), SubLayer 7a-7d, ContinuousEffect, EffectManager.\n   - `/workspace/test_utils.py`: test helpers (see concepts).\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_13/{card_impl,tests}.py`: target validation pattern — `get_targets` returns `[TargetRequirement(filter_fn=..., description=..., zone=Zone.BATTLEFIELD)]`; `on_resolve` reads `self.chosen_targets`. ContinuousEffect imported from engine.continuous_effects with `source/layer/sublayer/apply/duration`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_134/card_impl.py` (Ajani planeswalker): pattern for `get_loyalty_abilities()` returning `[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost=+1, effect=_plus1, description=...), ...]`; uses `getattr(pw, \"_resolve_target\", None)`; subclasses `Planeswalker`, sets `starting_loyalty`, adds Supertype.LEGEND