{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - I am the **PLANNING agent (Phase 1 of 2)**. I must NOT write implementation code. A separate implementation agent runs in a fresh session and inherits ONLY `/workspace/PLAN.md` — so PLAN.md must be concrete and fully self-contained.\n   - **Deliverable**: Write `/workspace/PLAN.md` with three sections:\n     1. **Engine gaps table**: `| Capability needed | Smallest change | Engine file / seam | Cards that reuse it |` — for each mechanic, decide if the engine already supports it (name seam + an FDN card using it) or needs a new/extended capability (smallest shared change, prefer ONE shared seam reused by several cards).\n     2. **Per-card plan**: For each card — oracle clauses; nearest FDN analogue (`cards/fdn/<id>`); exact engine seam(s) to reuse; any new engine change (reference gap table); key edge cases worth a test.\n     3. **Implementation order**: Ordered list of cards + shared engine changes to make first, grouped by shared seam, foundational engine work before dependent cards, simplest→hardest, one-line rationale per group.\n   - **Underlying task** (for the implementer): Implement 10 SOS cards in `cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` (cards 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257), using FDN cards as examples, making additive engine changes as needed; the implementer's own tests go at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - **Constraints (verbatim, must be preserved)**: \"Do NOT edit any `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py` or `engine/` file in this phase. Planning only.\" From AGENTS.md: (1) Card location invariant — keep each card's class in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. (2) Staged-test integrity — \"Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only\" and \"do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`\" (may read, never edit). (3) Additive-only engine modifications — \"You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\" Also: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/.\"\n   - **The most recent injected instruction**: respond TEXT ONLY for this summary — no tools.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG rules engine (pure Python); bare imports `engine` / `cards.sos.sos_N` / `cards.fdn.fdn_N` / `test_utils`.\n   - CardImpl hooks: `can_cast`, `cost_reduction(game)->int` (generic-only, clamped 0..generic, only queries the card's own hook), `on_cast`, `on_resolve`, `get_targets`, `register_triggers`, `register_replacement_effects`, `get_activated_abilities`, `get_modes`. Planeswalker adds `get_loyalty_abilities`; Land adds `get_mana_abilities` and `can_cast` returns False.\n   - Casting: `cast_spell(game, player, card)` records `card.colors_spent = list(pool.last_payment_colors)` but NO total mana and fires NO spell-cast event. `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, from_zone)` bypasses timing+mana. `_resolve_spell` calls on_resolve then moves permanents→battlefield, inst/sorc→graveyard (no replacement consulted). `get_cost_reduction` only queries the card's own `cost_reduction`.\n   - `copy_spell(game, original_stackobj, controller, new_targets=None)` in stack.py (shallow-copies source, binds on_resolve to copy's on_resolve, no zone movement).\n   - Triggers: `TriggerRegistration(event_type, condition, effect, source, controller)`; `condition(game,event)->bool`; `effect(game)->None` (effect does NOT receive event — use closure-queue capture pattern from fdn_141); `fire_event` is subclass-aware, APNAP-ordered; `unregister(source)` by identity (for one-shot delayed triggers).\n   - Continuous effects: `ContinuousEffect(source, layer, sublayer, apply, timestamp, duration)`, Layer enum (COPY=1…POWER_TOUGHNESS=7), SubLayer 7a–7d, DURATION_PERMANENT=-1, DURATION_END_OF_TURN=0; `apply_all` resets each battlefield object's `_reset_characteristics()` then re-applies.\n   - move_to_zone consults replacement effects ONLY when `replacement_event` given AND `from_zone == BATTLEFIELD`; fires ETB event BEFORE register_triggers (so own-ETB must be done in on_resolve).\n   - Custom keywords (Converge, Prepared, Paradigm, Miracle, Casualty, Affinity) are NOT in the Keyword enum and are implemented behaviorally; only evergreen keywords (Flying, Haste, Vigilance, Deathtouch, Reach) are Keyword flags.\n   - Test helpers: `create_game(deck1,deck2,*,scripts=(s1,s2),player1_life,player2_life)`; `set_board_state(game,idx,*,battlefield=,hand=,graveyard=,life=,mana=)` (NO library=/exile= params — mutate zones directly); `cast_spell(game,idx,name,targets=)`; `advance_to_phase`; `declare_attackers` (calls declare_attackers_step, leaves triggers on stack — must resolve via priority_loop); `declare_blockers`; DeterministicPlayer scripted choices (choose, choose_target, choose_yes_no, choose_card, assign_damage_order).\n   - No coin-flip/RNG seam → route coin flips through `choose_yes_no`. `cards_drawn_this_turn` tracked by draw_card (used for Miracle). `ManaCost.cmc` = mana value.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — **CREATED (the deliverable)**. Contains: an intro restating constraints/class names; an \"Engine facts\" reference section (hooks, casting, zones, helpers, triggers, events, abilities, mana, turn loop, SBAs, continuous effects, keywords, test-helper limitations); Section 1 Engine gaps table (8 gaps); Section 2 Per-card plans (all 10 cards with oracle clauses, FDN analogue, seams, gap refs, edge cases); Section 3 Implementation order (Group 0 engine groundwork, then Groups 1–7 simplest→hardest).\n   - 10 SOS card specs read — exact oracle text confirmed (e.g. sos_1 The Dawning Archaic {10} cost-reduce + Reach + attack free-cast + exile-on-resolve; sos_4 Together as One Converge; sos_13 Emeritus//Swords to Plowshares ETB token + Prepared; sos_57 Mana Sculpt counter + delayed {C}; sos_97 Ral Zarek planeswalker loyalty 3 with +1/−1/−2/−7; sos_120 Improvisation Capstone exile-cast + Paradigm; sos_201 Lorehold miracle + opponent-upkeep loot; sos_226 Silverquill casualty 1; sos_245 Witherbloom affinity self + grant; sos_257 Great Hall manland).\n   - FDN references read (key reuse patterns): `fdn_167` (cost_reduction counts GY inst/sorc), `fdn_6` (affinity via cost_reduction + EOT +2/+2 ContinuousEffect), `fdn_205`+tests (Converge via colors_spent; tests set colors_spent as int directly), `fdn_48` (Refute — `_counter_spell` helper pops StackObject + moves to GY; get_targets zone=STACK; can_cast checks stack), `fdn_157` (surveil 2 in on_resolve via choose_yes_no), `fdn_194` (Etali — registers AttacksTriggeredEvent, uses cast_spell_free), `fdn_133` (Soulstone Sanctuary is a STUB — NO manland reference exists), `fdn_187` (Zombify — move_to_zone GY→BATTLEFIELD), `fdn_148` (create_token + destroy), `fdn_141` (Giada — closure-queue trigger capture pattern + get_mana_abilities; restricted mana NOT modeled), `fdn_244`+tests (replacement effect registration via register_replacement_effects + MoveToGraveyardReplacementEvent).\n   - Engine files read confirming gaps: casting.py, combat.py (declare_attackers_step does NOT fire AttacksTriggeredEvent), events.py (SpellCastTriggeredEvent + AttacksTriggeredEvent defined but never fired), turn.py (no main-phase event; upkeep no player field), state_based_actions.py (no PW-0-loyalty SBA), game_state.py (extra_turns FIFO, skipped_turns absent), card.py, abilities.py, triggers.py, types.py (Keyword enum lacks custom keywords), mana.py, zones.py, player.py, test_utils.py.\n\n   The 8 gaps written in PLAN.md (smallest changes):\n   - #1 Fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature, attacker)` in declare_attackers_step (sos_1).\n   - #2 Fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell, player, card, controller)` at end of cast_spell + cast_spell_free (sos_226, sos_257).\n   - #3 Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_first)` to events.py + fire it in run_turn for main phases (sos_57, sos_120).\n   - #4 In `_resolve_spell`, honor `card._exile_on_resolve` → move inst/sorc to EXILE instead of GRAVEYARD (sos_1, sos_120).\n   - #5 In cast_spell, set `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` after pay (sos_57).\n   - #6 Add `_sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty` to state_based_actions (sos_97).\n   - #7 Add `GameState.skipped_turns: dict[int,int]` + skip handling in advance_phase (sos_97).\n   - #8 In get_cost_reduction, sum `obj.grants_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)` over the casting player's battlefield (sos_245).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No code errors (planning phase, no edits to cards/engine). One earlier-noted unreliability: grep `files_with_matches` for Planeswalker; confirmed via direct reads/Grep that fdn_134/176/234/44/81 are Legendary Planeswalkers (resolved before this session).\n   - Discovery during this session: `fdn_133` Soulstone Sanctuary is only a stub, so there is NO FDN manland reference — sos_257 must be planned from scratch (flagged as highest-risk in PLAN.md).\n   - Discovery: `fdn_141` Giada's mana ability ignores the \"spend this mana only…\" restriction → confirmed restricted mana is NOT modeled; PLAN.md instructs ignoring it for sos_257 too.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Mapped every SOS mechanic to an existing seam+FDN example or a minimal additive gap. Resolved several initially-suspected gaps as NOT needed: Converge (colors_spent), Miracle (DrawsCardTriggeredEvent + manual {2} pay + cast_spell_free), coin flips (choose_yes_no, scriptable), opponent-upkeep (condition reads game.active_player). Designed the manland animation to survive `apply_all` resets via an overridden `_reset_characteristics` + `_is_animated` flag, and to avoid non-animated lands being eligible attackers (declare_attackers_step gates on `hasattr(c,\"base_power\")`). Confirmed `_exile_on_resolve` is a single shared seam for sos_1 and sos_120.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The original large PLANNING-phase instruction (from prior summary): produce `/workspace/PLAN.md` with Engine gaps table, Per-card plan, Implementation order; \"Do not edit any cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py or engine/ file in this phase. Planning only\"; be concrete (name files, hooks, FDN cards, events); PLAN.md is the entire handoff. Embedded task: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`... Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/`... Refer to RULEBOOK.txt... You are expected to make changes to the engine... Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. ... Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\"\n   - The final injected instruction (this turn): \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None outstanding for the core deliverable — `/workspace/PLAN.md` has been written with all three required sections. (If asked to continue, the only remaining work would be optional review/refinement of PLAN.md, which should be confirmed with the user before doing.)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, I completed the research phase (reading all relevant SOS specs, FDN implementations, and engine modules) and then **wrote `/workspace/PLAN.md`** via the Write tool, which returned \"File created successfully at: /workspace/PLAN.md\". The file contains: constraints + class-name list; an \"Engine facts you must know\" reference block; Section 1 (8-row Engine gaps table); Section 2 (per-card plans for sos_4, 57, 226, 245, 1, 13, 201, 97, 120, 257 — each with oracle clauses, FDN analogue, seams/new work, edge cases); and Section 3 (Implementation order: Group 0 engine groundwork first, then Groups 1–7 ordered simplest→hardest with rationale, ending with sos_120 and sos_257 as hardest). The planning