{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set) Magic: The Gathering cards in a Python game engine at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` for collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. This is Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION, TDD, requirements-driven). Key directives:\n   - **The contract is the requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan.** PLAN.md is a guide/hypothesis written by an agent that couldn't run code — free to disagree with specific API/attribute claims when they don't match the real engine; jot a one-line note in PLAN.md when deviating.\n   - Use TDD: write one test through the public interface (test_utils), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green), repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time, not all tests up front). Write own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Validate against requirements before declaring done: re-read each oracle_text clause vs RULEBOOK.txt; run a throwaway real-engine smoke check; reuse nearest FDN seam; keep engine changes minimal/shared.\n   - Guardrails: test the real engine never a stand-in; after each card AND any engine/ change run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never regress it. **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/`** (grader uses its own authoritative copies; modifying workspace tests will not change score, only mislead).\n   - **Additive-only engine**: MAY add files/methods/classes/helpers in `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions; MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` (breaks grader imports). MUST NOT edit existing `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class stays in `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py` with fixed class names.\n   - Rules questions → grep RULEBOOK.txt (do not read whole).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Converge, Affinity for creatures, Casualty, Miracle, Prepared, Paradigm, Surveil, cost reduction, planeswalker loyalty abilities, counter target spell, manland animation, coin flips, skip turns.\n   - Engine architecture: CardImpl hook system, StackObject/Stack (LIFO), TriggerManager (APNAP, isinstance matching, closure-deque capture pattern), ReplacementManager (zone-change redirection), continuous effects 7-layer system, state-based actions, mana pool with last_payment_colors tracking.\n   - Custom keywords (Converge, Casualty, Miracle, Paradigm, Affinity, Prepared) are NOT Keyword enum values — implement behaviorally. Only evergreen keywords (FLYING, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH) set via Keyword flag.\n   - TDD via test_utils public interface (create_game, set_board_state, cast_spell, advance_to_phase, declare_attackers, declare_blockers).\n   - DeterministicPlayer scripts choices via a deque (_script); scripted answers feed choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card/assign_damage_order in pop order.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — The brief. Contains 8-gap engine table (Section 1), per-card plans (Section 2), implementation order (Section 3). I should add one-line notes here when deviating from the plan.\n   - `/workspace/AGENTS.md` — Hard rules (card location invariant, read-only engine_tests/, additive-only engine).\n   - `/workspace/engine/casting.py` — MODIFIED (3 edits):\n     - Gap #2: Added at end of `cast_spell` after `game.stack.push(stack_obj)`: fires `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player)` (import from engine.events).\n     - Gap #2: Same fire added at end of `cast_spell_free`.\n     - Gap #5: Added after `player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`: `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`.\n     - Gap #4: In `_resolve_spell`, instant/sorcery branch now: `elif getattr(card, \"_exile_on_resolve\", False): move_to_zone(game, card, Zone.STACK, Zone.EXILE)` before the graveyard else.\n     - Gap #8: In `get_cost_reduction`, after `raw = card.cost_reduction(game)`, added loop: `for obj in game.get_battlefield(controller).get_all(): grant = getattr(obj, \"grants_cost_reduction\", None); if grant is not None: raw += grant(game, card, controller)` before restoring controller and clamping.\n   - `/workspace/engine/combat.py` — MODIFIED (Gap #1): In `declare_attackers_step` for-loop, after tapping the attacker, added: `from engine.events import AttacksTriggeredEvent; game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game, AttacksTriggeredEvent(creature=attacker, attacker=attacker))`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/events.py` — MODIFIED (Gap #3): Added `@dataclass class BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(TriggeredEvent): player: Any = None; is_first: bool = False` before `BeginningOfCombatTriggeredEvent`. (SpellCastTriggeredEvent and AttacksTriggeredEvent already existed.)\n   - `/workspace/engine/turn.py` — MODIFIED (Gap #3): In `run_turn`, added branch after DRAW step: `elif game.phase in (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN) and game.step is None:` fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=game.active_player, is_first=(game.phase == Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN))`.\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py` — MODIFIED (Gap #6, PARTIAL): Added `_sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty(game)` function before `_sba_draw_from_empty_library`:\n     ```python\n     def _sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty(game: GameState) -> bool:\n         action_taken = False\n         to_remove: list[tuple[Player, Any]] = []\n         for player in game.players:\n             for obj in _battlefield(game, player).get_all():\n                 if (CardType.PLANESWALKER in getattr(obj, \"card_types\", set())\n                         and getattr(obj, \"loyalty\", 1) <= 0):\n                     to_remove.append((player, obj))\n         for player, obj in to_remove:\n             _move_to_grave