{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011hmvf6aLgDMADMYV4RU27F","type":"tool_result","content":"150\t    7. **Call on_cast** — invoke the card's ``on_cast`` hook.\n151\t    8. **Push StackObject** — push a :class:`StackObject` whose\n152\t       ``on_resolve`` callback handles resolution.\n153\t\n154\t    Raises:\n155\t        CastingError: If any legality check fails.\n156\t    \"\"\"\n157\t    # 1. Timing\n158\t    if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n159\t        raise CastingError(\n160\t            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n161\t        )\n162\t\n163\t    # 2. can_cast\n164\t    if not card.can_cast(game):\n165\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n166\t\n167\t    # 3. Hand check\n168\t    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n169\t    if not hand.contains(card):\n170\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not in hand\")\n171\t\n172\t    # 4. Move card from hand to stack zone\n173\t    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n174\t    hand.remove(card)\n175\t    stack_zone.add(card)\n176\t\n177\t    # Clear any stale colors_spent from a prior cast before new payment.\n178\t    if hasattr(card, \"colors_spent\"):\n179\t        del card.colors_spent\n180\t\n181\t    # 5. Choose targets\n182\t    target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n183\t    chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n184\t    if target_specs:\n185\t        for spec in target_specs:\n186\t            target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n187\t            # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n188\t            filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n189\t            if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n190\t                if not filter_fn(target):\n191\t                    stack_zone.remove(card)\n192\t                    hand.add(card)\n193\t                    raise CastingError(\n194\t                        f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n195\t                        f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n196\t                    )\n197\t            chosen_targets.append(target)\n198\t\n199\t    # 5b. Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this\n200\t    #     spell (the T in DEBT).\n201\t    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n202\t\n203\t    for target in chosen_targets:\n204\t        if has_protection_from(target, card):\n205\t            # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n206\t            stack_zone.remove(card)\n207\t            hand.add(card)\n208\t            raise CastingError(\n209\t                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n210\t            )\n211\t\n212\t    # Targets are stored on the StackObject (not the card) and passed\n213\t    # through the resolve pipeline via on_resolve(game, targets=...).\n214\t\n215\t    # 6. Mana check / payment (rollback on failure)\n216\t    # Ensure the card knows its controller so that cost_reduction() hooks\n217\t    # (e.g. Embercleave counting attacking creatures you control) see the\n218\t    # casting player, even for cards that were added to hand without an\n219\t    # explicit controller assignment.\n220\t    if card.controller is None:\n221\t        card.controller = player\n222\t    reduction = get_cost_reduction(game, card, player)\n223\t    effective_cost = _apply_cost_reduction(card.mana_cost, reduction) if reduction > 0 else card.mana_cost\n224\t\n225\t    if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n226\t        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n227\t        stack_zone.remove(card)\n228\t        hand.add(card)\n229\t        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — insufficient mana\")\n230\t\n231\t    # TODO: Phase 3 — support player choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\n232\t    player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n233\t\n234\t    # Record how much mana was spent to cast this spell so that effects which\n235\t    # care (e.g. Mana Sculpt) can read it later.  X-cost spells undercount X.\n236\t    card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n237\t\n238\t    # Store colors of mana spent on the card for mechanics like Converge\n239\t    # that care about the colors used to cast the spell.\n240\t    card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n241\t\n242\t    # 7. Call on_cast hook\n243\t    card.on_cast(game)\n244\t\n245\t    # 8. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n246\t    stack_obj = StackObject(\n247\t        source=card,\n248\t        controller=player,\n249\t        targets=chosen_targets,\n250\t        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n251\t    )\n252\t\n253\t    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n254\t        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n255\t\n256\t    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n257\t    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n258\t\n259\t    # Fire the spell-cast event so \"whenever you cast …\" triggers (and\n260\t    # casualty-style abilities) can respond.  Spell copies are created via\n261\t    # copy_spell and pushed directly, so they do not re-enter this path —\n262\t    # no infinite recursion.\n263\t    from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n264\t\n265\t    game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n266\t        game,\n267\t        SpellCastTriggeredEvent(\n268\t            spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player\n269\t        ),"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feeb00d4-a69a-45e3-8d4a-c1e07df7c37b","uuid":"44d71c84-943c-49b9-9552-2ac7ad93088d","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:13:04.747Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/engine/casting.py","content":"    7. **Call on_cast** — invoke the card's ``on_cast`` hook.\n    8. **Push StackObject** — push a :class:`StackObject` whose\n       ``on_resolve`` callback handles resolution.\n\n    Raises:\n        CastingError: If any legality check fails.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Timing\n    if not can_cast_at_instant_speed(card) and not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n        raise CastingError(\n            f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n        )\n\n    # 2. can_cast\n    if not card.can_cast(game):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — can_cast returned False\")\n\n    # 3. Hand check\n    hand = game.get_hand(player)\n    if not hand.contains(card):\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — card not in hand\")\n\n    # 4. Move card from hand to stack zone\n    stack_zone = player.zones[Zone.STACK]\n    hand.remove(card)\n    stack_zone.add(card)\n\n    # Clear any stale colors_spent from a prior cast before new payment.\n    if hasattr(card, \"colors_spent\"):\n        del card.colors_spent\n\n    # 5. Choose targets\n    target_specs = card.get_targets(game)\n    chosen_targets: list[Any] = []\n    if target_specs:\n        for spec in target_specs:\n            target = player.choose_target(target_specs, spec)\n            # Validate against filter_fn if the spec provides one\n            filter_fn = getattr(spec, \"filter_fn\", None)\n            if filter_fn is not None and target is not None:\n                if not filter_fn(target):\n                    stack_zone.remove(card)\n                    hand.add(card)\n                    raise CastingError(\n                        f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — chosen target does not \"\n                        f\"satisfy filter: {getattr(spec, 'description', '')}\"\n                    )\n            chosen_targets.append(target)\n\n    # 5b. Protection check — reject targets that have protection from this\n    #     spell (the T in DEBT).\n    from engine.protection import has_protection_from\n\n    for target in chosen_targets:\n        if has_protection_from(target, card):\n            # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n            stack_zone.remove(card)\n            hand.add(card)\n            raise CastingError(\n                f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — target has protection from this spell\"\n            )\n\n    # Targets are stored on the StackObject (not the card) and passed\n    # through the resolve pipeline via on_resolve(game, targets=...).\n\n    # 6. Mana check / payment (rollback on failure)\n    # Ensure the card knows its controller so that cost_reduction() hooks\n    # (e.g. Embercleave counting attacking creatures you control) see the\n    # casting player, even for cards that were added to hand without an\n    # explicit controller assignment.\n    if card.controller is None:\n        card.controller = player\n    reduction = get_cost_reduction(game, card, player)\n    effective_cost = _apply_cost_reduction(card.mana_cost, reduction) if reduction > 0 else card.mana_cost\n\n    if not player.mana_pool.can_pay(effective_cost):\n        # Rollback: move card from stack zone back to hand\n        stack_zone.remove(card)\n        hand.add(card)\n        raise CastingError(f\"Cannot cast {card.name!r} — insufficient mana\")\n\n    # TODO: Phase 3 — support player choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\n    player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)\n\n    # Record how much mana was spent to cast this spell so that effects which\n    # care (e.g. Mana Sculpt) can read it later.  X-cost spells undercount X.\n    card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    # Store colors of mana spent on the card for mechanics like Converge\n    # that care about the colors used to cast the spell.\n    card.colors_spent = list(player.mana_pool.last_payment_colors)  # type: ignore[attr-defined]\n\n    # 7. Call on_cast hook\n    card.on_cast(game)\n\n    # 8. Build on_resolve callback and push StackObject\n    stack_obj = StackObject(\n        source=card,\n        controller=player,\n        targets=chosen_targets,\n        on_resolve=lambda g: None,  # replaced below\n    )\n\n    def _on_resolve(g: GameState) -> None:\n        _resolve_spell(g, card, player, stack_obj)\n\n    stack_obj.on_resolve = _on_resolve\n    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n\n    # Fire the spell-cast event so \"whenever you cast …\" triggers (and\n    # casualty-style abilities) can respond.  Spell copies are created via\n    # copy_spell and pushed directly, so they do not re-enter this path —\n    # no infinite recursion.\n    from engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n\n    game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n        game,\n        SpellCastTriggeredEvent(\n            spell=stack_obj, player=player, card=card, controller=player\n        ),","numLines":120,"startLine":150,"totalLines":525}}}
