{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set) Magic: The Gathering cards in a Python game engine at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` for collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. This is Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION, TDD, requirements-driven). Key directives:\n   - **The contract is the requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan.** PLAN.md is a guide/hypothesis written by an agent that couldn't run code — free to disagree with specific API/attribute claims when they don't match the real engine; jot a one-line note in PLAN.md when deviating.\n   - Use TDD: write one test through the public interface (test_utils), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green), repeat vertically (one tracer bullet at a time). Write own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Validate against requirements: re-read each oracle_text clause vs RULEBOOK.txt; run throwaway real-engine smoke checks; reuse nearest FDN seam; keep engine changes minimal/shared.\n   - Guardrails: test the real engine never a stand-in; after each card AND any engine/ change run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never regress it. **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/`** (grader uses its own authoritative copies; modifying workspace tests will not change score, only mislead).\n   - **Additive-only engine**: MAY add files/methods/classes/helpers in `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions; MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` (breaks grader imports). MUST NOT edit existing `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class stays in `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py` with fixed class names.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Converge, Affinity for creatures, Casualty, Miracle, Prepared, Paradigm, Surveil, cost reduction, planeswalker loyalty, counter target spell, manland animation, coin flips, skip turns.\n   - Engine: CardImpl hook system (can_cast, cost_reduction, on_cast, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, get_activated_abilities, get_loyalty_abilities, get_mana_abilities), StackObject/Stack (LIFO, `_items`, `.objects()`, `.push()`, `.pop()`, `.is_empty()`), TriggerManager (APNAP, isinstance matching, `register(TriggerRegistration)`, `unregister(source)`, `fire_event` pushes StackObject with `on_resolve=trigger.effect`), ReplacementManager, continuous effects 7-layer system, SBAs, ManaPool (`add`, `get`, `can_pay`, `pay`, `last_payment_colors`, `total`).\n   - Custom keywords (Converge, Casualty, Miracle, Paradigm, Affinity, Prepared) are NOT Keyword enum values — implement behaviorally. Only evergreen (FLYING, HASTE, VIGILANCE, DEATHTOUCH, REACH) set via Keyword flag.\n   - `colors_spent` set as LIST of Color in real cast (casting.py:240) but as INT in fdn reference tests — handle both: `cs if isinstance(cs, int) else len(cs)`.\n   - ETB ordering: `_resolve_spell` calls `on_resolve` BEFORE moving card to battlefield, so ETB self-counts need +1.\n   - `cards_drawn_this_turn` is NEVER reset by the engine (only incremented in draw_card) — unusable for \"first draw this turn\"; track per-turn draws on the source via `game.turn_number` comparison.\n   - Activated ability convention (from fdn_114): `cost(game, src) -> bool` (checks+pays), `effect(game) -> None`, target read via `src._current_target`.\n   - `_get_chosen_target(card)`: `chosen = getattr(card,\"chosen_targets\",None); return chosen[0] if chosen else getattr(card,\"_resolve_target\",None)`.\n   - test_utils: `create_game(deck1,deck2,scripts=...)`, `set_board_state(game,idx,battlefield=,hand=,graveyard=,life=,mana=)`, `cast_spell(game,idx,name,targets=)` (requires empty stack; scripts targets to front of DeterministicPlayer `_script`), `advance_to_phase`, `declare_attackers` (appendleft attackers), `declare_blockers`. DeterministicPlayer pops scripted answers via `_script` deque for choose/choose_target/choose_yes_no/choose_card.\n   - Library `top` = last element (`_objects[-n:]`); to make a card drawn first, add it last.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/engine/state_based_actions.py` — MODIFIED: wired planeswalker SBA. Added line in `check_state_based_actions`: `# Planeswalker with 0 or less loyalty → graveyard\\n    action_taken = _sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty(game) or action_taken` after the lethal-damage check. (`_sba_planeswalker_zero_loyalty` function already existed.)\n   - `/workspace/engine/game_state.py` — MODIFIED (gap #7): Added in `__init__` after `_normal_next_index`: `self.skipped_turns: dict[int, int] = {}`. In `advance_phase` end-of-turn normal-rotation else branch replaced with: `candidate = self._normal_next_index; self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index; while self.skipped_turns.get(candidate, 0) > 0: self.skipped_turns[candidate] -= 1; candidate = self._normal_next_index; self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index; self.active_player_index = candidate`.\n   - Prior engine edits (from earlier summary, confirmed present): casting.py (gap #2 SpellCastTriggeredEvent in cast_spell & cast_spell_free; gap #5 `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc`; gap #4 `_exile_on_resolve`; gap #8 `grants_cost_reduction` loop in `get_cost_reduction`); combat.py (gap #1 AttacksTriggeredEvent); events.py (gap #3 BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent); turn.py (gap #3 fire BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent at main phase).\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `TogetherAsOne(Sorcery)`, {6}. Helper `_converge_count(card)` handles int/list. `get_targets` returns [player TargetRequirement, any-target TargetRequirement]. `on_resolve`: X=converge count; chosen[0] player draws X; chosen[1] deal_damage X; controller.life += X + fire GainsLifeTriggeredEvent.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py` — CREATED, 3 tests pass.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)`, {6}{B}{G}, 5/5, {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, LEGENDARY, FLYING|DEATHTOUCH. `cost_reduction` = creatures you control. `grants_cost_reduction(self, game, card, controller)` returns creatures-you-control count if card is INSTANT/SORCERY else 0. Helper `_creatures_you_control`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py` — CREATED, 8 tests pass.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `TheDawningArchaic(Creature)`, {10}, 7/7, {\"Avatar\"}, LEGENDARY, REACH. `cost_reduction` counts inst/sorc in gy. `register_triggers` registers AttacksTriggeredEvent trigger (`_condition: event.creature is source`); `_effect`: gather inst/sorc in gy, choose_yes_no, choose card, set `chosen._exile_on_resolve = True`, `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`. Helper `_is_instant_or_sorcery`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py` — CREATED, 6 tests pass. Uses `_QuickStudy(Sorcery)` with `resolved` flag and `_drain_stack` helper.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)`, {2}{W}{B}, 4/4, {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, LEGENDARY, FLYING|VIGILANCE. `register_triggers` on SpellCastTriggeredEvent: condition checks caster is controller + spell is inst/sorc (reads `event.spell` which is the StackObject, `.source` is the card), stores `_pending_card`. Effect: gather creatures power>=1, choose_yes_no, choose sac, find original StackObject in `game.stack._items` by `so.source is pending_card`, `sacrifice`, optionally new targets via `_choose_new_targets`, `copy_spell` + push. Module helper `_choose_new_targets(game, ctrl, original_so)`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` — CREATED, 7 tests pass. Uses `_Ping(Sorcery)` dealing 3 to opponent.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `ManaSculpt(Instant)`, {1}{U}{U}. Helpers `_get_chosen_target`, `_counter_spell` (pop from `game.stack._items`, remove from controller STACK zone, add to owner graveyard), `_controls_wizard`, `_schedule_mana` (registers one-shot BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent trigger with `source=object()` token, effect adds COLORLESS mana then `unregister(token)`). `can_cast`/`get_targets` (zone=STACK). `on_resolve`: capture `mana_spent` from countered card, counter, if Wizard+mana_spent>0 schedule mana.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` — CREATED, 6 tests pass. Helpers `_push_victim` (builds victim Sorcery + StackObject, pushes, sets mana_spent) and `_drain`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares(Creature)`, {1}{W}{W}, 3/3, {\"Cat\",\"Cleric\"}, NOT legendary, `self._is_prepared=False`. `get_targets` = target player. `on_resolve`: create 1/1 FLYING Inkling token for target player, count creatures (with +1 self if not yet on battlefield), set `_is_prepared=True` if any opponent has more. `get_activated_abilities` returns one ability: cost gates on `_is_prepared` + pays {W}; effect exiles `_current_target`, target's controller gains life=power, sets `_is_prepared=False`. Helper `_creature_count`.\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — CREATED, 11 tests pass.\n   - `/workspace/PLAN.md` — MODIFIED: added `[DEVIATION]` note in sos_13 section that spec type_line is \"Creature — Cat Cleric\" (NOT Legendary), so implemented without Supertype.LEGENDARY.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Write tool error on sos_226 and sos_1 card_impl.py: \"File has not been read yet.\" Fix: Read the stub file first, then Write. (Stubs must be Read before Write per harness rules.)\n   - No test failures encountered — all cards passed on first green attempt after red confirmation.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Determined `colors_spent` dual int/list handling; verified via real-cast smoke check (3 colors → X=3, draws 3, deals 3, gains 3 life).\n   - Confirmed `cards_drawn_this_turn` never resets → designed Lorehold miracle to track per-turn draws on the source via turn_number comparison.\n   - Engine groundwork complete (gaps #1-#8); full suite 1184 passed; engine_tests + cards/sos 1169 passed after 4 cards.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial message was a system-reminder dump of Read tool results for state_based_actions.py, turn.py, events.py, game_state.py (partial), plus notes about casting.py/combat.py and deferred tools. (The actual task prompt and prior context are in the prior summary; no NEW free-text user instruction in this session beyond system reminders.)\n   - A \"Tool loaded\" system message after ToolSearch listing tasks #1-#11.\n   - Repeated task-tool reminder system messages (gentle reminders to track tasks).\n   - The final message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools...\" requesting this summary.\n   - Security/constraint instructions preserved verbatim from task: \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\" Also: MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine items; MUST NOT edit existing fdn tests.py; card class stays in fixed location with fixed class name.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Task #8 (in_progress): sos_201 Lorehold, the Historian ({3}{R}{W} 5/5 Flying/Haste Legendary Dragon; miracle {2} for inst/sorc in hand; opponent-upkeep loot discard-then-draw).\n   - Task #9: sos_97 Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer ({1}{B}{B} Legendary PW loyalty 3; +1 surveil 2, -1 any number of target players discard, -2 reanimate cmc<=3, -7 coin flips/skip turns — needs gaps #6, #7).\n   - Task #10: sos_120 Improvisation Capstone ({5}{R}{R} sorcery; exile top until cmc>=4 free-cast; Paradigm self-copy).\n   - Task #11: sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land; mana abilities; {5} animation to 2/4 Wizard; cast-inst/sorc +1/+0 EOT pump).\n   - Final validation: run full `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` (and cards/sos) to confirm no regressions after all cards.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Was implementing sos_201 Lorehold (task #8, in_progress). Read the spec: \"Flying, haste\\nEach instant and sorcery card in your hand has miracle {2}. (You may cast a card for its miracle cost when you draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn.)\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, you may discard a card. If you do, draw a card.\" {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Legendary Elder Dragon, Flying|Haste. Designed two triggers:\n   1. Miracle on DrawsCardTriggeredEvent: condition checks `event.player is controller`, tracks per-turn draws on source (`source._miracle_last_turn`/`_miracle_draws`, reset when `game.turn_number` changes), only fires when `_miracle_draws == 1` AND card is inst/sorc; effect: if card still in hand, choose_yes_no, can_pay/pay ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\"), `cast_spell_free(game, ctrl, card, Zone.HAND)`.\n   2. Loot on BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent (empty dataclass — no player field): condition `game.active_player is not controller`; effect: choose_yes_no, if hand non-empty choose_card → discard → draw_card.\n   Just inspected `ZoneContainer.top` (returns `_objects[-n:]`, top=last element) and `add` to plan library seeding for the test. Stub class name is `LoreholdTheHistorian` (per PLAN line 14 conventions — needs verification of exact stub class name before writing). Had NOT yet written the sos_201 test or implementation.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` stub to confirm the exact class name, then write `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` (red) covering: properties (name, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, Flying+Haste, Legendary, Elder Dragon), miracle fires on first-draw inst/sorc (deals damage via free-cast bolt with {2} paid), miracle NOT on second draw, opponent-upkeep loot (discard→draw), and no loot on controller's own upkeep — then implement `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` with the two triggers described above, run green, then run engine_tests to confirm no regression. This directly continues task #8 which was in_progress. Per PLAN: \"register_triggers registers two triggers: 1. Miracle on DrawsCardTriggeredEvent ... 2. Loot on BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent: condition — game.active_player is not <controller>\". Note deviation from PLAN's `cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` check (that field never resets) — instead track per-turn draws on the source.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/feeb00d4-a69a-45e3-8d4a-c1e07df7c37b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feeb00d4-a69a-45e3-8d4a-c1e07df7c37b","uuid":"216cdb4a-c682-48fc-b398-d58ef5bb5239","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:27:56.601Z","isSynthetic":true}
