{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013zroGnNS8zh1tNVWx2r9Es","type":"tool_result","content":"406\t### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)  — needs gaps #3, #4  — *hardest, do last with sos_257*\n407\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile\n408\t  cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of them without\n409\t  paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n410\t  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its\n411\t  mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n412\t- **FDN analogue:** exile-top + free-cast `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali).\n413\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop the controller's\n414\t  library top repeatedly (`zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`), `move_to_zone(card,\n415\t  Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`, accumulate `card.mana_cost.cmc`, stop once the\n416\t  running total `>= 4` (or library empties). For each exiled **nonland** card,\n417\t  offer `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)` gated on\n418\t  `choose_yes_no` (verbatim Etali loop). **Paradigm:** set\n419\t  `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4**, so Capstone exiles itself instead of\n420\t  going to the graveyard), and register an ongoing trigger on\n421\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**) with `source=self`,\n422\t  condition `event.player is controller and event.is_first`; effect — optionally\n423\t  (`choose_yes_no`) cast a **copy** of the exiled Capstone for free. Implement the\n424\t  copy with a small local helper that mirrors `engine/stack.py copy_spell`: shallow\n425\t  `copy.copy(self)`, set `owner/controller`, build a `StackObject` whose\n426\t  `on_resolve` calls the copy's `on_resolve`, and push it (the copy is a one-shot\n427\t  effect, not a real card in a zone, so don't worry about its post-resolution zone).\n428\t- **Edge cases:** exiling stops exactly when cumulative cmc ≥ 4 (one big card can\n429\t  satisfy it alone); lands among the exiled cards aren't castable; Capstone ends in\n430\t  **exile** (assert), not graveyard; the Paradigm trigger only fires on the\n431\t  controller's **first** (precombat) main phase, repeatedly each turn; the recurring\n432\t  copy re-runs the exile-and-cast effect. Verify the trigger is registered after\n433\t  resolution, then fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller,\n434\t  is_first=True)` and resolve.\n435\t\n436\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n437\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n438\t  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n439\t  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n440\t  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n441\t- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n442\t  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n443\t  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n444\t  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n445\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n446\t  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n447\t    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n448\t    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n449\t    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n450\t  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feeb00d4-a69a-45e3-8d4a-c1e07df7c37b","uuid":"3db4fa90-1426-40d2-a905-2ce7a6c9d6aa","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:35:51.666Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_120 — Improvisation Capstone  ({5}{R}{R} Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm)  — needs gaps #3, #4  — *hardest, do last with sos_257*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile\n  cards with total mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of them without\n  paying their mana costs. Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve\n  a spell with this name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its\n  mana cost at the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\"\n- **FDN analogue:** exile-top + free-cast `cards/fdn/fdn_194` (Etali).\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Sorcery`. `on_resolve`: pop the controller's\n  library top repeatedly (`zones[Zone.LIBRARY]`), `move_to_zone(card,\n  Zone.LIBRARY, Zone.EXILE)`, accumulate `card.mana_cost.cmc`, stop once the\n  running total `>= 4` (or library empties). For each exiled **nonland** card,\n  offer `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)` gated on\n  `choose_yes_no` (verbatim Etali loop). **Paradigm:** set\n  `self._exile_on_resolve = True` (**gap #4**, so Capstone exiles itself instead of\n  going to the graveyard), and register an ongoing trigger on\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (**gap #3**) with `source=self`,\n  condition `event.player is controller and event.is_first`; effect — optionally\n  (`choose_yes_no`) cast a **copy** of the exiled Capstone for free. Implement the\n  copy with a small local helper that mirrors `engine/stack.py copy_spell`: shallow\n  `copy.copy(self)`, set `owner/controller`, build a `StackObject` whose\n  `on_resolve` calls the copy's `on_resolve`, and push it (the copy is a one-shot\n  effect, not a real card in a zone, so don't worry about its post-resolution zone).\n- **Edge cases:** exiling stops exactly when cumulative cmc ≥ 4 (one big card can\n  satisfy it alone); lands among the exiled cards aren't castable; Capstone ends in\n  **exile** (assert), not graveyard; the Paradigm trigger only fires on the\n  controller's **first** (precombat) main phase, repeatedly each turn; the recurring\n  copy re-runs the exile-and-cast effect. Verify the trigger is registered after\n  resolution, then fire `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller,\n  is_first=True)` and resolve.\n\n### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`","numLines":45,"startLine":406,"totalLines":539}}}
