{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GRQ7ZDZLEDEgWqTTYaNrgg","type":"tool_result","content":"436\t### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n437\t- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n438\t  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n439\t  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n440\t  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n441\t- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n442\t  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n443\t  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n444\t  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n445\t- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n446\t  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n447\t    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n448\t    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n449\t    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n450\t  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`\n451\t    whose `cost` checks the land isn't already a creature and pays `{5}`\n452\t    (`controller.mana_pool.can_pay/pay(ManaCost(generic=5))`), and whose `effect`\n453\t    turns it into a creature **permanently**. Because `effect_manager.apply_all`\n454\t    calls `_reset_characteristics()` (which on a base `CardImpl` resets\n455\t    `card_types`/`keywords` to originals) the transformation must survive resets.\n456\t    Cleanest contained approach: set a flag `self._is_animated = True`; give this\n457\t    class the creature surface so the engine treats it as a creature **while\n458\t    animated** — define instance attrs (`base_power=2, base_toughness=4,\n459\t    modified_power, modified_toughness, damage_marked=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n460\t    minus_one_counters=0, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n461\t    summoning_sick=False`) and `power`/`toughness` properties (modified + counters)\n462\t    on the class; and **override `_reset_characteristics`** to call\n463\t    `super()._reset_characteristics()` then, if `self._is_animated`, re-add\n464\t    `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype `\"Wizard\"` and reset `modified_power/toughness`\n465\t    to 2/4. Do **not** predefine `base_power` before animation (so a non-animated\n466\t    land is not picked up as an attacker by `declare_attackers_step`, which gates on\n467\t    `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`); set those attrs in the animation `effect`.\n468\t  - **Granted trigger:** the \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, +1/+0 EOT\"\n469\t    ability uses **gap #2** (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). Register it in\n470\t    `register_triggers` (fires on the land's ETB); condition — `self._is_animated`,\n471\t    `event.controller is self.controller`, `event.card` is inst/sorcery; effect —\n472\t    add an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n473\t    sublayer=MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN, apply=lambda g:\n474\t    setattr(self, \"modified_power\", self.modified_power + 1))` (mirror `fdn_6`).\n475\t- **This is the highest-risk card** — write thorough unit tests: produces {C};\n476\t  pays 1 life for any color (life drops by 1); `{5}` flips it to a 2/4 Wizard\n477\t  creature that is still a land (`CardType.LAND` and `CardType.CREATURE` both\n478\t  present); animation is idempotent across `effect_manager.apply_all()` /\n479\t  cleanup (call `apply_all` and assert it's still a 2/4 creature); the pump adds\n480\t  +1/+0 per inst/sorc cast and resets at end of turn; a **non-animated** land is\n481\t  not a legal attacker.\n482\t\n483\t---\n484\t\n485\t## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n486\t\n487\tEngine changes are small and additive; landing them first de-risks the cards.\n488\tWithin each group, build the card, write its `tests.py`, and run `pytest` (confirm\n489\t`engine_tests/` + FDN tests stay green) before moving on.\n490\t\n491\t**Group 0 — Engine groundwork (do all first).** Land gaps #1–#8 from Section 1 in\n492\tone pass and run the full suite. They don't depend on each other and every one is a\n493\tfew lines. Rationale: cards below assume these seams exist; landing them together\n494\tlets you verify the regression suite once and then focus purely on card logic.\n495\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"feeb00d4-a69a-45e3-8d4a-c1e07df7c37b","uuid":"35e7ba0e-a885-4dcc-92b4-c086271bee38","timestamp":"2026-06-04T12:38:30.329Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/PLAN.md","content":"### sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex  (Land)  — needs gap #2  — *hardest, do last*\n- **Oracle clauses:** \"{T}: Add {C}. {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\n  Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell. {5}: If this isn't a\n  creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with 'Whenever you cast an instant or\n  sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.' It's still a land.\"\n- **FDN analogue:** mana abilities + ignored mana restriction `cards/fdn/fdn_141`\n  (Giada: `get_mana_abilities` returning `ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced,\n  description)`; the \"spend only on …\" restriction is **not modeled** there, so\n  ignore it here too); EOT pump pattern `cards/fdn/fdn_6`.\n- **Seams + new work:** subclass `Land`.\n  - `get_mana_abilities()` returns two `ManaAbility`s: (1) `cost = tap_cost`,\n    `mana_produced` adds `ManaType.COLORLESS` 1; (2) `cost` taps + pays 1 life\n    (`controller.life -= 1`), `mana_produced` adds one mana of a color the\n    controller chooses (`controller.choose`). Ignore the spend-restriction.\n  - **Animation ({5}):** `get_activated_abilities()` returns an `ActivatedAbility`\n    whose `cost` checks the land isn't already a creature and pays `{5}`\n    (`controller.mana_pool.can_pay/pay(ManaCost(generic=5))`), and whose `effect`\n    turns it into a creature **permanently**. Because `effect_manager.apply_all`\n    calls `_reset_characteristics()` (which on a base `CardImpl` resets\n    `card_types`/`keywords` to originals) the transformation must survive resets.\n    Cleanest contained approach: set a flag `self._is_animated = True`; give this\n    class the creature surface so the engine treats it as a creature **while\n    animated** — define instance attrs (`base_power=2, base_toughness=4,\n    modified_power, modified_toughness, damage_marked=0, plus_one_counters=0,\n    minus_one_counters=0, is_attacking=False, is_blocking=False,\n    summoning_sick=False`) and `power`/`toughness` properties (modified + counters)\n    on the class; and **override `_reset_characteristics`** to call\n    `super()._reset_characteristics()` then, if `self._is_animated`, re-add\n    `CardType.CREATURE` + subtype `\"Wizard\"` and reset `modified_power/toughness`\n    to 2/4. Do **not** predefine `base_power` before animation (so a non-animated\n    land is not picked up as an attacker by `declare_attackers_step`, which gates on\n    `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")`); set those attrs in the animation `effect`.\n  - **Granted trigger:** the \"whenever you cast an instant or sorcery, +1/+0 EOT\"\n    ability uses **gap #2** (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`). Register it in\n    `register_triggers` (fires on the land's ETB); condition — `self._is_animated`,\n    `event.controller is self.controller`, `event.card` is inst/sorcery; effect —\n    add an end-of-turn `ContinuousEffect(source=self, layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS,\n    sublayer=MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN, apply=lambda g:\n    setattr(self, \"modified_power\", self.modified_power + 1))` (mirror `fdn_6`).\n- **This is the highest-risk card** — write thorough unit tests: produces {C};\n  pays 1 life for any color (life drops by 1); `{5}` flips it to a 2/4 Wizard\n  creature that is still a land (`CardType.LAND` and `CardType.CREATURE` both\n  present); animation is idempotent across `effect_manager.apply_all()` /\n  cleanup (call `apply_all` and assert it's still a 2/4 creature); the pump adds\n  +1/+0 per inst/sorc cast and resets at end of turn; a **non-animated** land is\n  not a legal attacker.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 — Implementation order\n\nEngine changes are small and additive; landing them first de-risks the cards.\nWithin each group, build the card, write its `tests.py`, and run `pytest` (confirm\n`engine_tests/` + FDN tests stay green) before moving on.\n\n**Group 0 — Engine groundwork (do all first).** Land gaps #1–#8 from Section 1 in\none pass and run the full suite. They don't depend on each other and every one is a\nfew lines. Rationale: cards below assume these seams exist; landing them together\nlets you verify the regression suite once and then focus purely on card logic.\n","numLines":60,"startLine":436,"totalLines":539}}}
