{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Implement 10 SOS (set) Magic: The Gathering cards in a Python game engine at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py` for collector numbers 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257. This is Phase 2 (IMPLEMENTATION, TDD, requirements-driven). Key directives (preserved verbatim from prior task context):\n   - **The contract is the requirements (card_spec.json + RULEBOOK.txt), NOT the plan.** PLAN.md is a guide/hypothesis written by an agent that couldn't run code — free to disagree with specific API/attribute claims when they don't match the real engine; jot a one-line note in PLAN.md when deviating.\n   - Use TDD: write one test through the public interface (test_utils), watch it fail (red), write minimal code (green), repeat vertically. Write own tests at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n   - Validate against requirements: re-read each oracle_text clause vs RULEBOOK.txt; reuse nearest FDN seam; keep engine changes minimal/shared.\n   - Guardrails: test the real engine never a stand-in; after each card AND any engine/ change run `python3 -m pytest engine_tests/ -q` — never regress it. **Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/`** (grader uses its own authoritative copies; modifying workspace tests will not change score, only mislead). \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading.\"\n   - **Additive-only engine**: MAY add files/methods/classes/helpers in `engine/` and MAY modify bodies of existing functions; MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/` (breaks grader imports). MUST NOT edit existing `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py`.\n   - Card location invariant: each card's class stays in `cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py` with fixed class names.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG mechanics: Converge, Affinity, Casualty, Miracle, Prepared, Paradigm, Surveil, cost reduction, planeswalker loyalty, counter target spell, manland animation, coin flips, skip turns.\n   - Engine hooks: can_cast, cost_reduction, on_cast, on_resolve, get_targets, register_triggers, get_activated_abilities, get_loyalty_abilities, get_mana_abilities, _reset_characteristics.\n   - StackObject/Stack (`_items`, `.objects()`, `.push()`, `.pop()`, `.is_empty()`), TriggerManager (`register(TriggerRegistration)`, `unregister(source)`, `get_triggers_for_source(source)`, `fire_event` calls `condition(game, event)` exactly once per matching trigger then pushes StackObject with on_resolve=trigger.effect; APNAP ordering).\n   - EffectManager (continuous_effects.py): `add(ContinuousEffect)`, `remove_expired(game)` (sweeps DURATION_END_OF_TURN), `apply_all(game)` (calls `_reset_objects` → `_reset_characteristics()` on each battlefield permanent, then applies sorted effects). ContinuousEffect(source, layer=Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=SubLayer.MODIFY_PT, apply, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN).\n   - Creature surface: base_power/base_toughness, modified_power/modified_toughness, plus_one_counters/minus_one_counters, damage_marked, is_tapped, summoning_sick, is_attacking, is_blocking; `power = modified_power + plus_one_counters - minus_one_counters`; `_reset_characteristics` resets card_types to `_original_card_types` snapshot, keywords, modified_power=base_power, etc.\n   - `draw_card` fires DrawsCardTriggeredEvent(player, card); increments `cards_drawn_this_turn` but NEVER resets it → track per-turn draws on source via `game.turn_number` comparison.\n   - `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent()` has NO fields; whose upkeep = `game.active_player`. `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, is_first)`. `SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=stack_obj, player, card, controller)`.\n   - Planeswalkers: subclass Planeswalker(starting_loyalty=N); get_loyalty_abilities returns list[LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)]; abilities.py has LoyaltyAbilityInstance, activate_ability, AbilityError, clear_loyalty_tracking (module-global `_loyalty_activated_this_turn` set keyed by (object_id, turn_number)); loyalty cost paid on activation, once-per-turn + sorcery-speed enforced; gap #6 SBA kills planeswalker at loyalty<=0.\n   - gap #7: `game.skipped_turns: dict[int,int]`; advance_phase end-of-turn rotation consumes skips (`_normal_next_index` starts at 1, active starts at 0).\n   - gap #4: `_resolve_spell` (casting.py:412) calls card.on_resolve, then moves STACK→EXILE if `_exile_on_resolve` else STACK→GRAVEYARD (or BATTLEFIELD for permanents).\n   - `ManaCost.cmc` property (types.py:164). Generic mana paid by any color. `is_sorcery_speed(game, player)` (active player + main phase + empty stack).\n   - Attacker eligibility gates on `hasattr(c, \"base_power\")` (combat.py:228, :297) — so a non-animated manland must NOT define base_power until animated.\n   - Activated ability convention: `cost(game, src) -> bool` (checks+pays), `effect(game) -> None`. ManaAbility(cost, mana_produced, description). LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description).\n   - `_resolve_target` backdoor (fdn cards) for test-set targets; `_get_chosen_target` reads chosen_targets[0] or `_resolve_target`.\n   - test_utils: create_game(deck1, deck2, scripts=(s1,s2)), set_board_state(game, idx, battlefield=/hand=/graveyard=/life=/mana=), DeterministicPlayer._script deque popped via choose/choose_yes_no/choose_card/choose_target. Library top = last element (`get_all()[-1]`); add() appends.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` — CREATED. `LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)`, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5, {\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}, LEGENDARY, FLYING|HASTE. Helper `_is_instant_or_sorcery`. register_triggers registers two triggers:\n     - Miracl